# direnv: enter flake.nix's devshell on cd, so `direnv exec . <cmd>` works in a sandbox
# (where `nix develop` cannot reach the daemon socket). Needs `direnv allow .` once, from an
# unsandboxed shell.
#
# This is `devShells.default`, which is `rust-worker-stack` — Rust + wasm, Cloudflare worker
# tooling, Aiken, Mithril, and the agent toolkit including `skill-store`. nix-direnv caches it, so
# the first entry is the slow one. A lighter shell is `nix develop .#<name>` for the one job you
# are doing.
use flake
